---
import LangBlock from "@/components/LangBlock.astro";
import T from "@/components/T.astro";
import { t } from "@/i18n/ui";
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";

const meta = {
	description:
		"Open-source projects and personal experiments in DevOps, Kubernetes, and Infrastructure automation",
	title: t("en", "page.projects"),
	titleDe: t("de", "page.projects"),
};
---

<PageLayout meta={meta}>
	<h1 class="title mb-12"><T tKey="projects.heading" /></h1>
	<LangBlock>
		<Fragment slot="en">
			<div class="prose prose-sm prose-cactus max-w-none">
				<p class="mb-8 text-lg">
					Here are some of the projects I've built to learn, experiment, and solve real-world
					infrastructure problems. All code is open-source on my GitHub!
				</p>

				<!-- Featured Projects -->
				<div class="space-y-10">
					<!-- Canary Deployment Strategy -->
					<div class="border-accent-2 rounded-lg border p-6 transition-shadow hover:shadow-lg">
						<div class="mb-4 flex items-start justify-between">
							<h2 class="!mt-0 !mb-2">Canary Deployment on Kubernetes</h2>
							<a
								class="cactus-link text-sm"
								href="https://github.com/shptk/CanaryDeployK8S"
								rel="noreferrer"
								target="_blank"
							>
								View on GitHub →
							</a>
						</div>

						<p class="mb-4">
							A complete implementation of canary deployment strategy using Terraform and Kubernetes
							manifests. Because rolling out changes without proper testing is... brave? Reckless?
							You decide.
						</p>

						<h3 class="!mb-2 text-base">What's Inside:</h3>
						<ul class="mb-4 list-inside list-disc space-y-1">
							<li>Infrastructure as Code using Terraform for K8s cluster setup</li>
							<li>Canary deployment manifests with traffic splitting</li>
							<li>Automated rollback mechanisms</li>
							<li>Monitoring integration to track canary health</li>
						</ul>

						<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
							<span
								class="bg-accent-2/10 text-accent-2 inline-block rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold"
								>Kubernetes</span
							>
							<span
								class="bg-accent-2/10 text-accent-2 inline-block rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold"
								>Terraform</span
							>
							<span
								class="bg-accent-2/10 text-accent-2 inline-block rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold"
								>DevOps</span
							>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Ansible Jenkins Integration -->
					<div class="border-accent-2 rounded-lg border p-6 transition-shadow hover:shadow-lg">
						<div class="mb-4 flex items-start justify-between">
							<h2 class="!mt-0 !mb-2">Ansible Jenkins CI/CD Pipeline</h2>
							<a
								class="cactus-link text-sm"
								href="https://github.com/shptk/Ansible-Jenkins-Integration"
								rel="noreferrer"
								target="_blank"
							>
								View on GitHub →
							</a>
						</div>

						<p class="mb-4">
							End-to-end Infrastructure as Code and CI/CD setup for a Flask application. This
							project automates the entire journey from infrastructure provisioning to application
							deployment.
						</p>

						<h3 class="!mb-2 text-base">Features:</h3>
						<ul class="mb-4 list-inside list-disc space-y-1">
							<li>Automated Jenkins server configuration using Ansible</li>
							<li>Kubernetes cluster setup and configuration</li>
							<li>Complete CI/CD pipeline for Flask application</li>
							<li>Configuration management and deployment automation</li>
							<li>Integration testing and deployment verification</li>
						</ul>

						<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
							<span
								class="bg-accent-2/10 text-accent-2 inline-block rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold"
								>Ansible</span
							>
							<span
								class="bg-accent-2/10 text-accent-2 inline-block rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold"
								>Jenkins</span
							>
							<span
								class="bg-accent-2/10 text-accent-2 inline-block rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold"
								>Kubernetes</span
							>
							<span
								class="bg-accent-2/10 text-accent-2 inline-block rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold"
								>Flask</span
							>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- More Projects Coming Soon -->
					<div class="border-accent-2 rounded-lg border border-dashed p-6 opacity-60">
						<h2 class="!mt-0 !mb-2">More Projects Coming Soon</h2>
						<p class="mb-0">
							I'm constantly tinkering with new ideas and technologies. Check back soon for more
							projects, or better yet, follow me on <a
								class="cactus-link inline-block"
								href="https://github.com/shptk"
								rel="noreferrer"
								target="_blank">GitHub</a
							> to see what I'm working on!
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Call to Action -->
				<div class="border-accent-2 mt-12 border-t-2 pt-8">
					<h2>Interested in Collaborating?</h2>
					<p>
						I'm always open to collaborating on interesting DevOps and infrastructure projects. If
						you have an idea or want to contribute to any of my existing projects, feel free to
						reach out or open an issue on GitHub!
					</p>
					<div class="mt-4 flex gap-4">
						<a
							class="cactus-link inline-block"
							href="https://github.com/shptk"
							rel="noreferrer"
							target="_blank"
						>
							GitHub Profile →
						</a>
						<a class="cactus-link inline-block" href="mailto:shashwatpathak100@gmail.com">
							Email Me →
						</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</Fragment>
		<Fragment slot="de">
			<div class="prose prose-sm prose-cactus max-w-none">
				<p class="mb-8 text-lg">
					Einige Projekte, die ich gebaut habe, um zu lernen, zu experimentieren und echte
					Infrastruktur-Probleme zu lösen. Der Code ist durchgehend Open Source auf GitHub.
				</p>

				<!-- Featured Projects -->
				<div class="space-y-10">
					<!-- Canary Deployment Strategy -->
					<div class="border-accent-2 rounded-lg border p-6 transition-shadow hover:shadow-lg">
						<div class="mb-4 flex items-start justify-between">
							<h2 class="!mt-0 !mb-2">Canary Deployment auf Kubernetes</h2>
							<a
								class="cactus-link text-sm"
								href="https://github.com/shptk/CanaryDeployK8S"
								rel="noreferrer"
								target="_blank"
							>
								Auf GitHub ansehen →
							</a>
						</div>

						<p class="mb-4">
							Eine vollständige Umsetzung der Canary-Deployment-Strategie mit Terraform und
							Kubernetes-Manifesten. Denn Änderungen ohne ordentliches Testen auszurollen ist
							… mutig? Fahrlässig? Entscheiden Sie selbst.
						</p>

						<h3 class="!mb-2 text-base">Was drinsteckt:</h3>
						<ul class="mb-4 list-inside list-disc space-y-1">
							<li>Infrastructure as Code mit Terraform für das Aufsetzen des K8s-Clusters</li>
							<li>Canary-Deployment-Manifeste mit Traffic-Splitting</li>
							<li>Automatisierte Rollback-Mechanismen</li>
							<li>Monitoring-Anbindung zur Überwachung der Canary-Instanz</li>
						</ul>

						<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
							<span
								class="bg-accent-2/10 text-accent-2 inline-block rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold"
								>Kubernetes</span
							>
							<span
								class="bg-accent-2/10 text-accent-2 inline-block rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold"
								>Terraform</span
							>
							<span
								class="bg-accent-2/10 text-accent-2 inline-block rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold"
								>DevOps</span
							>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Ansible Jenkins Integration -->
					<div class="border-accent-2 rounded-lg border p-6 transition-shadow hover:shadow-lg">
						<div class="mb-4 flex items-start justify-between">
							<h2 class="!mt-0 !mb-2">CI/CD-Pipeline mit Ansible und Jenkins</h2>
							<a
								class="cactus-link text-sm"
								href="https://github.com/shptk/Ansible-Jenkins-Integration"
								rel="noreferrer"
								target="_blank"
							>
								Auf GitHub ansehen →
							</a>
						</div>

						<p class="mb-4">
							Ein durchgängiges Setup aus Infrastructure as Code und CI/CD für eine
							Flask-Anwendung. Das Projekt automatisiert den gesamten Weg vom Bereitstellen der
							Infrastruktur bis zum Deployment der Anwendung.
						</p>

						<h3 class="!mb-2 text-base">Funktionen:</h3>
						<ul class="mb-4 list-inside list-disc space-y-1">
							<li>Automatisierte Konfiguration des Jenkins-Servers mit Ansible</li>
							<li>Aufsetzen und Konfigurieren des Kubernetes-Clusters</li>
							<li>Vollständige CI/CD-Pipeline für die Flask-Anwendung</li>
							<li>Konfigurationsmanagement und Deployment-Automatisierung</li>
							<li>Integrationstests und Verifikation des Deployments</li>
						</ul>

						<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
							<span
								class="bg-accent-2/10 text-accent-2 inline-block rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold"
								>Ansible</span
							>
							<span
								class="bg-accent-2/10 text-accent-2 inline-block rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold"
								>Jenkins</span
							>
							<span
								class="bg-accent-2/10 text-accent-2 inline-block rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold"
								>Kubernetes</span
							>
							<span
								class="bg-accent-2/10 text-accent-2 inline-block rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold"
								>Flask</span
							>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- More Projects Coming Soon -->
					<div class="border-accent-2 rounded-lg border border-dashed p-6 opacity-60">
						<h2 class="!mt-0 !mb-2">Weitere Projekte folgen</h2>
						<p class="mb-0">
							Ich probiere ständig neue Ideen und Technologien aus. Schauen Sie bald wieder vorbei
							— oder folgen Sie mir direkt auf <a
								class="cactus-link inline-block"
								href="https://github.com/shptk"
								rel="noreferrer"
								target="_blank">GitHub</a
							>, um zu sehen, woran ich gerade arbeite.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Call to Action -->
				<div class="border-accent-2 mt-12 border-t-2 pt-8">
					<h2>Lust auf Zusammenarbeit?</h2>
					<p>
						Für spannende DevOps- und Infrastruktur-Projekte bin ich immer offen. Wenn Sie eine Idee
						haben oder zu einem meiner bestehenden Projekte beitragen möchten, melden Sie sich gern
						oder öffnen Sie ein Issue auf GitHub.
					</p>
					<div class="mt-4 flex gap-4">
						<a
							class="cactus-link inline-block"
							href="https://github.com/shptk"
							rel="noreferrer"
							target="_blank"
						>
							GitHub-Profil →
						</a>
						<a class="cactus-link inline-block" href="mailto:shashwatpathak100@gmail.com">
							E-Mail schreiben →
						</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</Fragment>
	</LangBlock>
</PageLayout>
